    "chunk_size_bytes": 1890,
    "chunk_text": "4. With a view to formalize the distribution of films in national films industry, Cinema halls, which at present screenlocal films will be operated as three distribution channels by way of dividing them in to three categories. (Annex06) However for the purpose of screening a special film on the request of producer (Annex 07), Corporation willtake action depending on the situation to appoint maximum number of cinema halls attaching cinema halls in onechannel to another channel on the written approval of the Chairman depending on the recommendations of schedulingcommittee and recommendations made based on the criteria of Evaluation Board.\n\n6. The opportunity is given to screen either a local or imported film at another screening times in addition to theminimum screening times of the local film, which is scheduled for screening at cinema halls maintained under theabove three channels.\n\n7. Further imported films will be screened at cinema halls, in which imported films are screened, outside the channelsin which local films are screened. (Annex 8)\n\n8. Opportunity will be given to screen local films depending on the requests made by Cinema Halls, which screenthose imported films.\n\n9. Films with classical - attractive characteristics, films with commercial-attractive characteristics, and films withthe combination of classical - attractive characteristics and commercial-attractive characteristics, which arecategorized by the aforesaid Evaluation Board, will be screened at Cinema Halls under three channels where localfilms are screened.\n\nAccordingly they will be scheduled so as to be distributed equally under three categories.\n\nChannel 1Channel 2Channel 3\n\nFirst instanceFilms with classical -Films withFilms with the coombinationattractivecommercial-attractiveof classical - attractivecharacteristicscharacteristicscharacteristics andcommercial-attractivecharacteristics"
